{"id":"2605.28763","authors":[{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a674284","name":"Yiheng Zhu","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a674285","name":"Kangle Deng","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a674286","user":{"_id":"62cd5c43299c0c2e0e437842","avatarUrl":"/avatars/8fa8511baf2d9bd95d3ba4535a5b3d69.svg","isPro":false,"fullname":"Jean-Philippe Fauconnier","user":"j4kn","type":"user","name":"j4kn"},"name":"Jean-Philippe Fauconnier","status":"claimed_verified","statusLastChangedAt":"2026-06-01T11:49:06.400Z","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a674287","name":"Inaki Navarro","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a674288","name":"Daiqing Li","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a674289","name":"Ava Pun","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a67428a","name":"Yinan Zhang","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a67428b","name":"Peiye Zhuang","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a67428c","name":"Xiaoxia Sun","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a67428d","name":"Maneesh Agrawala","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a67428e","name":"Kiran Bhat","hidden":false},{"_id":"6a17a639b4840f905a67428f","name":"Tinghui Zhou","hidden":false}],"mediaUrls":["https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/6039478ab3ecf716b1a5fd4d/k4rHQ04FcyT__h_GALtOw.mp4"],"publishedAt":"2026-05-27T00:00:00.000Z","submittedOnDailyAt":"2026-05-28T00:00:00.000Z","title":"CubePart: An Open-Vocabulary Part-Controllable 3D Generator","submittedOnDailyBy":{"_id":"6039478ab3ecf716b1a5fd4d","avatarUrl":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6039478ab3ecf716b1a5fd4d/_Thy4E7taiSYBLKxEKJbT.jpeg","isPro":true,"fullname":"taesiri","user":"taesiri","type":"user","name":"taesiri"},"summary":"Interactive 3D assets used in games and simulation are typically decomposed into specific semantic parts to support animation, physics, and scripted behaviors, yet most generative 3D models produce either monolithic meshes or arbitrary part decompositions that cannot be aligned with application-specific requirements. We present CubePart, a generative framework for open-vocabulary, part-controllable 3D mesh generation that exposes part structure as an explicit inference-time control signal. Given a global text prompt and a user-defined parts schema expressed as an open-ended list of part names, our method generates a set of meshes - one per schema element - that assemble into a coherent object while respecting the specified semantic structure. To enable this capability, we introduce a scalable data pipeline to construct a large open-vocabulary, part-labeled 3D dataset, along with a two-stage generative architecture that separates global shape synthesis from part-level decoding. We demonstrate that the resulting assets can be directly integrated into game engines and driven by animation and behavior scripts without manual post-processing. Project Page: https://cubepart.github.io/","upvotes":13,"discussionId":"6a17a639b4840f905a674290","projectPage":"https://cubepart.github.io/","ai_summary":"CubePart is a generative framework that creates 3D mesh assets with explicit part structures controlled by text prompts and user-defined schemas, enabling direct integration into game engines.","ai_keywords":["generative framework","open-vocabulary","part-controllable 3D mesh generation","part structure","inference-time control signal","semantic structure","scalable data pipeline","part-labeled 3D dataset","two-stage generative architecture","global shape synthesis","part-level decoding"],"ai_summary_model":"Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct","linkedModels":[{"author":"Roblox","authorData":{"_id":"62a3a163b5db00777be6a438","avatarUrl":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6438428526c25444413c54d1/zHEWe9jE0_osXQZ1f4tRl.png","fullname":"Roblox Corporation","name":"Roblox","type":"org","isHf":false,"isHfAdmin":false,"isMod":false,"plan":"enterprise","followerCount":470,"isUserFollowing":false},"downloads":0,"gated":false,"id":"Roblox/cubepart","availableInferenceProviders":[],"lastModified":"2026-05-28T18:26:37.000Z","likes":23,"pipeline_tag":"text-to-3d","private":false,"repoType":"model","isLikedByUser":false},{"author":"TrNi","authorData":{"_id":"67baa2daa3da7b358c75b52b","avatarUrl":"/avatars/af0355035c9af2e51ea317ddc9b04544.svg","fullname":"Ni","name":"TrNi","type":"user","isPro":false,"isHf":false,"isHfAdmin":false,"isMod":false,"isUserFollowing":false},"downloads":0,"gated":false,"id":"TrNi/efficient-cubepart3d","availableInferenceProviders":[],"lastModified":"2026-10-04T00:15:00.000Z","likes":2,"pipeline_tag":"text-to-3d","private":false,"repoType":"model","isLikedByUser":false}],"numTotalModels":2,"linkedDatasets":[],"numTotalDatasets":0,"linkedSpaces":[{"emoji":"🧩","id":"Roblox/cubepart-demo","running":false,"shortDescription":"Open-vocabulary part-controllable 3D mesh generation","featured":false},{"emoji":"🧩","id":"pifreak/cubepart-demo","running":true,"shortDescription":"Open-vocabulary part-controllable 3D mesh generation","featured":false},{"emoji":"🧩","id":"franckgastel/cubepart-demo","running":false,"shortDescription":"Open-vocabulary part-controllable 3D mesh generation","featured":false}],"numTotalSpaces":3}